OL,3,GNEWSAPM 'on the fence' in
OL,4,ABirmingham-Manchester debate
OL,5,
OL,6,FAndy Burnham has refused to be drawn on
OL,7,Fwhether Birmingham or Manchester
OL,8,Fdeserves to be called England's second
OL,9,Fcity, but concedes the former "might be
OL,10,Fnudging ahead".
OL,12,FThe prime minister and former mayor of
OL,13,FGreater Manchester joked he would "sit
OL,14,Fon the fence" when challenged over the
OL,15,Flong-running rivalry between the two
OL,16,Fcities.
OL,18,FSpeaking to BBC Midlands political
OL,19,Feditor Elizabeth Glinka at Number 10
OL,20,FNorth in Manchester, Burnham was asked
OL,21,Fwhether he could "finally admit that
OL,22,FBirmingham is the second city".
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,353,350,200,160,0,100
